  "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
